  "details": "As a dedicated VRChat user who frequently uses desktop mode, having customizable keybinds would greatly enhance the experience by allowing for quicker access to commonly used features and improved accessibility. Many desktop players would benefit from the ability to assign specific functions—such as gestures, toggling UI elements, or muting/unmuting—to custom keybinds. This feature could improve the flow and functionality for desktop users and bring more parity between VR and desktop mode interactions.\n\nCustomizable Key Mapping: Allow users to map actions (e.g., sitting, crouching, dancing, gesture selection) to specific keys based on their preferences.\n\nProfile Saving: Let users save different keybind profiles, enabling quick switching between setups (e.g., one profile for chatting, another for exploring).\n\nUI Accessibility Shortcuts: Add shortcuts for opening the UI, social menus, and settings, making it easier to navigate in desktop mode without relying on mouse controls.\n\nEnhanced User Experience: Providing keybinds would enhance ease of use for non-VR players, giving them a more intuitive experience, especially for repetitive actions.",
